WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.887
Many applications need structured data rather than prose.

00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:10.667
For the duplicate-charge example, we can require three fields: category, urgency, and summary.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:15.992
We can also define the allowed values before generation.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:19.887
A useful output might classify the request as billing, assign medium urgency,

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:26.872
and summarize that a duplicate charge occurred and a refund was requested.

00:00:26.872 --> 00:00:32.201
Because the structure is explicit, the application can validate it before using it.
